course: dictionary
lesson: 10137
title: Threshold: a doorway, a level, a beginning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A threshold is the strip of wood or stone at the bottom of a doorway. It is the point where you step from outside into a room or house. Crossing the threshold means going through that doorway. Here the word is a real thing you can touch and see.
explain: The word also means the level or amount where something starts to happen or change. A pain threshold is the point where pain starts to feel too much. Clue words such as above, below and passing tell you that a number or mark is being used as the cut-off. Above the threshold, something happens; below it, it does not.
explain: «ne cherez porih» means «not across the threshold». Many families still avoid handing things or shaking hands across a doorway, so you step inside first. The custom shows that the threshold is a special line, not just a piece of wood.
explain: The third meaning is about beginnings. «On the threshold of» something means it is just about to begin. If a sentence says a scientist is on the threshold of a big discovery, the discovery is close but not yet made. Read the words around it to find out which meaning fits.
fact: A threshold is the strip at the bottom of a doorway.
fact: «ne cherez porih» means «not across the threshold», and many families still avoid handing things across a doorway.
fact: In science and maths, a threshold is a cut-off number: water boils above a threshold temperature.
fact: «On the threshold of» means something is just about to begin.
fact: Synonyms have similar meanings but different strength: a threshold is a starting line, while a limit is the furthest point you can go.
exercise: What is a threshold in a house? | *The strip at the bottom of a doorway | The top of the stairs | The kitchen cupboard | The window on the roof
exercise: «on the threshold of a big discovery» means the discovery is | Too small to see | *About to begin | Already finished last year | Lost in a cave
exercise: In a maths test, what does «above the threshold» mean? | *Reaching the cut-off mark or higher | Lying flat on the floor | Written in red ink | Below the cut-off mark
test: A pain threshold is | Where pain stops completely | The name of a hospital ward | *The point where pain starts to feel too much
test: In «ne cherez porih», the word threshold means | *The doorway you step across | A table in the kitchen | A window at the top of a wall
exam: Which phrase means something big is about to begin? | *On the threshold of | Above the threshold | Cross the threshold | Pain threshold
